**IMPORTANT - v4 onwards**

Callers **must** use an appropriate JSON parser to parse the output. **Do not** use any sort of simple pattern matching or regular expression-based solution.

The order of fields in the JSON output is not guaranteed and REKKI may add new fields any time.

**UPDATE TO REFLECT V4 CHANGES**

### The output payload structure has changed:

- Fields `inserted_at, inserted_at_ts, confirmed_by` were added
  - `confirmed_by` can be null
- Field `external_po_number` will always be present in the output, but can be null
- `size` field was added to the order items. It was previously obtainable via an optional input parameter.
- An `integration` field has been added, containing two nested fields:
  - `status`, which can be `pending`, `failed` or `success`
  - `integrated_at`, which will show the timestamp of a successful integration or be null otherwise.

In general, all fields will always be present, though certain fields can have null values. Check each field specification for details.

### The input payload structure has changed:

- Removed the `skip_integrated`, `show_previous_attempts` and `extra_item_fields` fields.
- Added a `filter` field.
  - currently has a nested `integration_statuses` field, which can be used to specify the statuses of the orders to be listed.
  - by default, no filter is applied.

Orders are limited to 1 month old at a maximum, i.e. if `since` contains an older timestamp, it will be disregarded and a limit of 1 month will be used.

